{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-evidence` skill MUST tell agents not to write placeholder evidence for a requirement or example whose implementation is pending.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The `habeas-evidence` skill MUST tell agents not to write placeholder evidence for a requirement or example whose implementation is pending.\n\nThe test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_never_writes_placeholder_evidence_for_pending_work]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It does the following:\n- It locates the \"Stop and report each finding that needs the user\" step in the bundled `habeas-evidence` skill's Workflow section, using the helpers `step_of`, `step` and `workflow_steps`.\n- It asserts with `assert_text_in_order` that the step's text contains \"names only implementation that is still pending\" and then, after it, \"never write placeholder evidence\".\n- The helpers panic if the step, the Workflow section or a phrase is missing, so the assertions are enforced.\n\nThe skill text in `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` (Workflow, step 6) reads: \"a missing record or false judgment whose rationale names only implementation that is still pending, which is expected. Don't keep iterating on those, and never write placeholder evidence.\" The test's ordered phrases tie the prohibition to the pending-implementation case. Removing or rewording the prohibition, or moving it out of that step, would fail the test.\n\nThe neighbouring test `the_evidence_skill_reports_findings_expected_while_implementation_is_pending` covers the related reporting guidance. It is not needed for this requirement.\n\nThe requirement has no other MUST, SHOULD or boundary cases. No gaps found.",
